<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila says Oct-Nov reserve money below programme.</title>
<headline>Manila says Oct-Nov reserve money below programme.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Central Bank said on Monday reserve money stood at 200.2 billion pesos during the October-November test period, 10 billion pesos below the programmed level.</p>
<p>The Central Bank regularly tracks the movement of reserve money during the last five working days of a month and first five working days of a month.</p>
<p>Reserve money is the sum of money in circulation.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
